- **Commit bodies not rewritten.** Twenty-nine bodies went out inexact, or became so as later commits changed the code, and pushed history is not rewritten. `e67fef9`'s "rebuild benchmarks" were a probe never committed, the shapes held since by `ObjectScanBenchmarks`; `b09f981` shipped its lexer's searches without a benchmark, `StreamEndSearchBenchmarks` holding them since, and its "a long line costs what searching it costs" holds of a long token, not of a line of short ones; `d63f093` and `7c0748b` say each run of white space is crossed once, false where an `/XRefStm`'s search tried two places or more, until `2b26d18`; `394028c` says a stream the `/XRefStm` read is taken only where its own `/Prev` names an older section, where any `/Prev` it gave sufficed; `5656c64` says an `/XRefStm` naming what its `/Prev` names outside the file, where the count guard ends the chain, is the guard's, where its test and the code say "outside the file", as a whole read does; `2b26d18` says whether a `/Prev` keeps its place is told by reading the object as the chain would, false within `MaxTrailerLength` of the window's edge until `f0d90c8`; `ea348ce` says where the reads part the data changes nothing, true of whole reads only until `cfaa90c`; `8ccd868` says the reports say which of the rows they count do not stand, which they leave unnamed, as `056461b` corrected the pages; `f0d90c8` says a section past a run of white space is looked for nearby as before, true of a `/Prev` or an `/XRefStm`, the section `startxref` names being rebuilt; `8ba4589` says the `limit.trailer` summary had the section always looked for near the offset, where that summary said nothing of white space; `8692234` says a table whose rest cannot be known keeps its words, false past 4,096 lost ranges, and gives "every object where the stream kept no row" for a split by the rows it holds; `de12b13` says the word is taken anywhere on its line, where it is taken wherever its line, lexed alone, reads it as a token; `092b772` says such a stream hands its `/Prev` on and has its numbers refused, true of a stream of `/Type /XRef` alone, that a stream whose value a guard cut is found unreadable for such data, false for a cut `/Size` or whole `/Index` until `5d10a36`, and that the look at a `/Prev`'s place drops what its decoding reported, false for a guard until `42ca0bb`; `ed61728` drops the same qualifier; `253f179` says the threat model's entry for the gap cites the tests, which its row of defenses does; `5de20b7` and `da0e157` are false beside a cut value until `68a55fa`; `d8e67de` gives an older revision's stream before the one the `/XRefStm` read as ending the chain, true only where it gives no `/Prev`, and places read at most 64 times a document, leaving out the look at the `/Prev`'s place past the bound; `9823992` spells judgment the British way; `68a55fa` says the look reports nothing, a guard its decoding reached standing since `e157359`, and `e3d0c99` says what decoding a dropped place's data reported goes with it, where a guard that decoding reached stands, as the comment it wrote says, and went out while the look dropped the guard its decoding beside a cut value reached, which `e157359` keeps; `b55738a` says nothing is reported where a limit stopped the chain or cut what it reached, false for the white-space guard until `5395eed`; `2be5c44` says a link inside a stream's number reads the same dictionary and data from there, false where the digits from there read 0; `220eab4` says a guard a decoding meets again is never counted left out, true only where the document holds its report and the decoding made fewer reports than the capacity before it; `305c1fb`, `78885bf` and `5880c0b` give the flag's reach as a dictionary a guard cut, any cut since `9e20161`; `69731a2` says the threat model's entry and three of its rows changed, where two did. Three source texts went out inexact too, each corrected since: `9823992`'s remark that a header counts only where its number starts a token, false for the walk back from `obj`, which finds `+17` or `x17` at its first digit, until `2be5c44`; `daca13c`'s summary that a guard a decoding meets again is not counted left out, scoped in `a0e94ca` to a decoding that made fewer reports than the capacity before it; and `7b1de15`'s, which gave the flag's reach as a cut inside the name a `/Type` gives, where the code takes any name `XRef` begins with wherever the cut fell, until `1c1d270`.
